2. MLOps-Specific Skills & Tools

Containerization & Orchestration

Tool	What You Need to Know	Importance	
Docker	Build images, package models, guarantee reproducibility	⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐	
Kubernetes	Pods, deployments, scaling, config maps, inference workloads	⭐⭐⭐⭐	

Experiment Tracking & Model Management
- MLflow: The open-source standard for tracking runs, model registry, and packaging
- Weights & Biases (W&B): Strong for collaboration and hyperparameter search
- DVC: Data version control — versions datasets alongside code commits

CI/CD for ML
ML CI/CD is fundamentally different from software CI/CD. Key differences:
- What changes: Code + data + model weights (not just code)
- Tests: Add model quality tests + data quality tests
- Artifacts: Docker image + model weights + config
- Rollback triggers: Metric degradation, data drift (not just errors)

Pipeline Architecture:

```
Code Change → Linting + Unit Tests → Data Validation → Model Training 
→ Model Evaluation (offline metrics + regression tests + fairness checks) 
→ Model Registry → Staging Deployment → Canary (5% traffic) → Full Rollout
```

Monitoring & Drift Detection
Three Types of Drift you must know:
1. Data Drift (Covariate Shift): Input distribution changes (e.g., model trained on US English gets Spanish queries)
2. Concept Drift: Relationship between inputs and outputs changes (e.g., holiday season shifts recommendations)
3. Model Performance Drift: Accuracy degrades even without data drift

Monitoring Stack:
- Evidently AI / WhyLabs: Drift detection
- Prometheus + Grafana: System metrics (latency, error rates)
- Arize / Fiddler: ML-specific observability

